WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.240
Each receptor reports on its own patch.

2
00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:07.640
So how does the eye mark an edge?

3
00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:09.600
Neighbours compare.

4
00:00:10.333 --> 00:00:13.073
The horseshoe crab, Limulus, has a compound eye.

5
00:00:13.993 --> 00:00:17.833
Each unit, an ommatidium, sends its own fibre into the optic nerve.

6
00:00:18.833 --> 00:00:22.193
Hartline, Wagner and Ratliff recorded one ommatidium.

7
00:00:23.233 --> 00:00:24.673
Steady light gave a steady discharge.

8
00:00:25.717 --> 00:00:27.617
Then they lit its neighbours as well.

9
00:00:28.397 --> 00:00:29.397
The discharge fell.

10
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:33.040
Was that the circuit at work?

11
00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.280
Or just stray light inside the eye?

12
00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:44.270
They cut the lateral connections to the recorded unit.

13
00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:47.390
The neighbours' light no longer inhibited it.

14
00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:50.750
The inhibition ran through connections between units.

15
00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:56.230
Think of each unit as reporting its own light, minus a share of its neighbours'

16
00:00:56.230 --> 00:00:57.230
light.

17
00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:01.490
Now take a row of units at an edge, dim on the left and bright on the right.

18
00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:04.210
The row continues beyond both ends.

19
00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:06.170
The numbers stay on screen.

20
00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:12.673
Deep inside each uniform region, every unit is inhibited by neighbours just like

21
00:01:12.673 --> 00:01:15.113
itself. Both plateaus drop.

22
00:01:16.117 --> 00:01:18.237
Now the dim unit right beside the edge.

23
00:01:19.097 --> 00:01:20.317
One of its neighbours is bright.

24
00:01:21.217 --> 00:01:22.997
Will it sit above its plateau, or below?

25
00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:32.510
Below. Its bright neighbour inhibits it more.

26
00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:37.410
And the bright unit at the edge sits above its plateau, because one neighbour is

27
00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:38.410
dim.

28
00:01:38.633 --> 00:01:43.913
What changed? The step across the edge is the same size as the input step.

29
00:01:44.867 --> 00:01:47.007
But the uniform regions now differ less.

30
00:01:47.767 --> 00:01:49.367
So the edge stands out against them.

31
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:56.620
The full model of the crab eye uses each neighbour's output, and the result still

32
00:01:56.620 --> 00:02:00.660
holds. In the vertebrate retina, other cells build the surround.

33
00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:06.190
Lateral inhibition discounts uniform regions, so differences stand out.

34
00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:07.750
Neighbours compare.
